  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P:$ A square has exactly four sides.\n\n- $Q:$ $7+2\\ge 10$\n\n- $R:$ $9$ is a prime number.",
  "worked_solution": "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *true.* Indeed, A square has exactly four sides.\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *false* because $7+2=9≱10.$\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $9$ is not a prime number (it is a composite number).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ only.\"",
